# RGJ-B5-001..006 — RecordStore target storage integration specification
#
# Source basis: current FreeJ2ME devel RecordStore semantics. Do not replace
# record IDs/tags/version/listener/auth/migration behavior.
#
# 1. Remove RG35XX-target dependence on java.nio.file.Files. Any helper using
#    Files.readAllBytes/copy/move must have java.io equivalents on this target.
#
# 2. Make RecordStore implement RG35XXRmsCoordinator.FlushableStore only on the
#    integrated source branch (interface is harmless cross-target if desired).
#
# 3. Split existing saveRecordStore() into:
#      byte[] serializeRecordStoreSnapshot()
#      void flushRG35XX()
#    Serialization must preserve the exact upstream file format.
#
# 4. For RG35XX/libretro target, mutation sites that currently call
#    saveRecordStore() synchronously (addRecord/setRecord/deleteRecord and any
#    equivalent metadata mutation) call:
#      RG35XXRmsCoordinator.getInstance().markDirty(this)
#    Non-RG35XX targets retain upstream synchronous behavior.
#
# 5. flushRG35XX() serializes a consistent snapshot under the same RecordStore
#    synchronization used for mutations, then releases the semantic lock before
#    physical I/O when safe. Persist through:
#      RG35XXRmsAtomicFile.write(file, snapshot)
#
# 6. Force-flush barriers:
#    - before final close clears in-memory vectors
#    - MIDlet pause/destroy integration
#    - game unload / Libretro case 10 transition
#    - Java libretro shutdown/deinit
#    Call RG35XXRmsCoordinator.getInstance().forceFlush().
#
# 7. Startup recovery:
#    - target exists => target is authoritative; discard stale target.tmp.
#    - target missing + temp exists => only promote after existing parser accepts
#      the complete temp contents; never blindly rename an unvalidated temp.
#    - backup is a replacement safety artifact, not a second RecordStore format.
#
# 8. Logging:
#    RG35XX production path must not log Arrays.toString(record payload) or emit
#    per-mutation SD diagnostics. Aggregate/error logging only.
#
# 9. Failure:
#    background failure keeps the store dirty. forceFlush must surface the saved
#    failure instead of silently reporting persistence success.
#
# 10. Rollback:
#    restoring synchronous saveRecordStore() calls is valid if async persistence
#    fails device validation. Keep RG35XXRmsAtomicFile independently if it proves
#    safer than direct overwrite.
